{"id": "lib/l10n/app_en.arb:logFoodConsentBody1", "file": "lib/l10n/app_en.arb", "location": "logFoodConsentBody1", "text": "A scan sends the barcode to openfoodfacts.org, a free, open food database. They see the barcode and your IP address. Nothing about you, your meals or your health leaves this phone, and a barcode you have scanned before is answered from your own copy without asking them again.", "sha256": "5877a51da2995173ba4f6af5a2af74828bc28b3cfc10fa02ecce5b938241099e", "kind": "arb"}
{"id": "lib/l10n/app_en.arb:logFoodConsentBody2", "file": "lib/l10n/app_en.arb", "location": "logFoodConsentBody2", "text": "Their numbers are typed in by the public and a fair few of them are wrong, so anything that fails a sanity check is left blank rather than filled in. Everything it does fill in is yours to edit before you save.", "sha256": "b3c9591a9337e2d3cd5095fd913da3b5d88f74109b61b512aac45eb554163514", "kind": "arb"}
{"id": "lib/l10n/app_en.arb:logFoodConsentBody3", "file": "lib/l10n/app_en.arb", "location": "logFoodConsentBody3", "text": "You can turn this back off in Settings › Privacy. Typing the numbers off the pack works either way.", "sha256": "db57b44b64baa6b1b7b160774c352357663240d09d93777375c78433d3af6ff3", "kind": "arb"}
{"id": "lib/l10n/app_en.arb:logFoodAllowLookups", "file": "lib/l10n/app_en.arb", "location": "logFoodAllowLookups", "text": "Allow lookups", "sha256": "aa979a43fc0c9eea3633ed048c1ee3016c97c54b7e8f315eb3d7f1808d5a9be9", "kind": "arb"}
